        "created_at": 1794500133.0174599
      },
      "rev_n_2_e140e2_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_e140e2_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_e140e2",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic programming to keep track of the maximum monsters defeated up to each town.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500133.0174787
      },
      "rev_n_3_03621b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_03621b_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_03621b",
        "thought_text": "Simulated annealing to explore different combinations of monster defeats while avoiding local maxima.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500133.0174918
      },
      "rev_n_1_97a049_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_97a049_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_97a049",
        "thought_text": "The issue arises because the current implementation incorrectly adds `min(A[i+1], B[i])` inside the inner `if` condition, which leads to double-counting some monsters. Instead, this calculation should be done once after the outer loop completes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_97a049_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_6bedcac5fa",
        "created_at": 1794500143.0021982
      },
      "rev_n_2_e140e2_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_e140e2_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_e140e2",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic programming with state transition considering both scenarios for each hero: either defeating monsters in their own town or in the next town. Initialize dp array properly and update it based on the maximum monsters defeated up to each town while considering the constraints.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_e140e2_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ac1cb83345",
        "created_at": 1794500156.412395
      },
      "rev_n_3_03621b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_03621b_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_03621b",
        "thought_text": "The issue lies in the logic where the total number of monsters defeated is calculated. Instead of subtracting the minimum between the hero's ability and the available monsters, we should add this value to the total number of monsters defeated. This adjustment ensures that we correctly account for the maximum number of monsters each hero can defeat without exceeding their capacity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_03621b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_47b00a6c5f",
        "created_at": 1794500168.6095567
      },
      "rev_n_4_b68428_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_b68428_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_b68428",
        "thought_text": "The current approach incorrectly subtracts the minimum between the hero's ability and the available monsters instead of adding it. This leads to an underestimation of the total number of monsters defeated.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2181726331927257472",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500183.23913
      },
      "rev_n_5_34fce9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_34fce9_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_34fce9",
        "thought_text": "To fix the issue, the logic inside the loop should be updated to add the minimum of (A[i] + A[i + 1]) and B[i] to total_defeated. This ensures that each hero's contribution to defeating monsters is correctly accounted for.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2181726331927257472",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500183.2391465
      },
      "rev_n_6_626eac_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_626eac_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_626eac",
        "thought_text": "Additionally, it's important to handle edge cases, such as when there is only one hero or when the number of heroes is equal to the number of towns minus one. These scenarios require special handling to avoid index errors and ensure the algorithm works correctly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2181726331927257472",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500183.2391555
      },
      "rev_n_5_34fce9_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_34fce9_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_34fce9",
        "thought_text": "To fix the issue, the logic inside the loop should be updated to add the minimum of (A[i] + A[i + 1]) and B[i] to total_defeated. This ensures that each hero's contribution to defeating monsters is correctly accounted for without exceeding their capacity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2181726331927257472",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_34fce9_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0159e0ecf7",
        "created_at": 1794500193.3892844
      },
